[E0404] Error: `s` would hold a copy of a `String`
   ╭─[ err/332_var_pattern_copies/main.wip:9:13 ]
   │
 9 │     var (n, s) = p
   │             ┬    ┬  
   │             ╰─────── owns memory, so it is never copied
   │                  │  
   │                  ╰── a place, which keeps its value
   │ 
   │ Help: to take the value apart, move it
   │ 
   │ Note: the names of a `var` pattern are variables of their own, which hold their parts; a place gives its value up to them with `move`
───╯
